bejoin_spill_ppc32_O0.o, bejoin_spill_sparc32_O0.o, bejoin_handoff_ppc32_O2.o,
bejoin_handoff_mips32_O2.o -- PowerPC, SPARC and MIPS32 big-endian objects for
the option bejoin evidence and callers and option bejoinpass whole shapes of
GH-904 and GH-815 (tests/stages/kuna-bejoin-residue.xml).

What they are
  bejoin_spill.c at -O0: widen and uwiden widen an argument after a call,
  local returns a `long long t = x;` kept across a call, and local_hi and
  sign are the `int`s over the same values. clang -O0 spills the argument
  and reloads it into the second return register (`lwz r4,8(r31); srawi
  r3,r4,31`), and reloads both words of t from the frame.
  bejoin_handoff.c at -O2: to_dbl passes add64's pair straight on to
  `__floatundidf` (`bl add64; bl __floatundidf`), store writes both words of
  sum, wrap hands sum's pair back without a tail call, and sign_of reads only
  wrap's first register for `wrap(a, b) < 0`.

Why they are vendored
  CI has no PowerPC, SPARC or MIPS toolchain, and the assertions depend on the
  exact register choices.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0-1ubuntu1.1 on the host:

      clang --target=powerpc-linux-gnu -fno-pic -O0 -w -c bejoin_spill.c -o bejoin_spill_ppc32_O0.o
      clang --target=sparc-linux-gnu -fintegrated-as -O0 -w -c bejoin_spill.c -o bejoin_spill_sparc32_O0.o
      clang --target=powerpc-linux-gnu -fno-pic -O2 -w -c bejoin_handoff.c -o bejoin_handoff_ppc32_O2.o
      clang --target=mips-linux-gnu -fno-pic -mno-abicalls -O2 -w -c bejoin_handoff.c -o bejoin_handoff_mips32_O2.o

